+|   frame takes ~200 ms; at 0.5 ms it takes ~95 ms. Asking  |
+|   for 0.5 ms only while a frame is being written keeps    |
+|   the speed without pinning the whole system to a 2 kHz   |
+|   tick the rest of the time.                              |
+|                                                           |
+|   A process has a single timer resolution request, so     |
+|   leaving the last boost scope puts back the 1 ms that    |
+|   main_Windows.cpp asked for, rather than releasing it.   |
+\*---------------------------------------------------------*/
+#ifdef _WIN32
+static std::mutex   fury_timer_boost_mutex;
+static unsigned int fury_timer_boost_count = 0;
